Description: site, sysconfig: AArch64 ILP32 dist-packages of its own
 Debian's distutils-install-layout.diff and sysconfig-debian-schemes.diff
 give the interpreter /usr/local/lib/python3.X/dist-packages,
 /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages and (platlibdir not "lib") also
 /usr/lib/python3.X/dist-packages, and install into the first (pip,
 posix_local scheme) or /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages (deb_system scheme,
 setuptools' distutils with --install-layout=deb). For an interpreter built
 with --with-platlibdir=libilp32 these are the LP64 python3.X's
 directories: its extension modules would be tried (.abi3.so, .so) and
 ILP32 installs would land among LP64 ones.
 .
 With sys.platlibdir == "libilp32" only, use the ILP32 counterparts:
 /usr/local/libilp32/python3.X/dist-packages, /usr/libilp32/python3/dist-packages
 and /usr/libilp32/python3.X/dist-packages on sys.path, the first two as
 posix_local and deb_system purelib/platlib and in _distutils_system_mod.
 In a virtual environment the environment's lib/ and libilp32/
 site-packages (posix_venv purelib and platlib) are added for the
 environment's prefix only; Debian's code adds only lib/ (the same as
 platlib when platlibdir is "lib"). test_site expects the ILP32 list.
 Every other platlibdir, Debian's "lib" included, takes the unchanged code.
Author: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no

